     "C9-selected actual typed ownership/resource/call/lifetime annotations, inferred effect/order/authority facts, expanded profile rules, scoped grants and selected provider allocation/generation/cleanup/transfer contracts. These inputs precede ownership state analysis; an actual provider contract is not a claim that runtime checks or allocation executed. Local typed interfaces and refusal fixtures need no whole Types/Effects/Runtime acceptance or held C7/C12 execution. Additional SAFE2-SAFE5 analysis consumes actual Core control/evaluation/cleanup paths and source/generated origins, including structured acquire/body/cleanup lowering; Types supplies current initialization/ownership/resource/call/foreign declarations and required layout facts, while Effects supplies actual allocation/failure/blocking/cleanup/transfer behavior. Consume validated provider declarations plus the actual deterministic provider-selection record after compatibility decisions, with existing exact grants and selected Runtime memory/region/arena/linear/foreign/device contracts. Backend supplies early target/ABI/layout policy descriptors, not emitted artifacts. Bind bounds, initialized ranges, field offsets/padding/alignment/endianness and allocator identity to the actual typed/source/provider/target facts; missing required layout or other facts cannot be invented. C7 typed layout facts precede analysis; later C14 derived layouts are checked by handoff rather than required before analysis. Derive state/path facts instead of trusting supplied initialized/valid/closed flags. Keep provider declarations, compatible selection, grants and actual provider execution distinct, with every original per-rule refusal and emission/preservation obligation retained. Additional L10/L18 analysis consumes the owning primitive/control outcome and structured acquire/body/cleanup products plus actual checked memory-policy/ordering decisions. Core lowering and supplied initialized/closed/provider flags are not state analysis. Derive initialization, owner/borrow/region/allocator/range/sharing and linear/privileged-forget obligations from those typed/source/provider/grant facts, preserving safe/unsafe alternatives and source-specific static refusals. These facts precede verified MIR and later actual provider/API execution. Additional L6 capture analysis consumes actual verified Core structure and early inferred direct/latent actions. Derive the selected resource/type/lifetime/transfer/cloning premises independently for Effects3 before its combined handler decision; existing later memory-policy analysis still consumes checked Effects3. Captured linear resources, borrows, raw pointers, interrupt state, locks and FFI frames need actual profile-valid transfer or refusal, not a candidate flag treated as proof. No final handler interpretation, whole Effects5 acceptance or later target layout is required before producing these source-bound facts.",
