  "- [ ] `release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/build-reproducible-signed-distributions-with-provenancesbom` Build reproducible signed distributions with provenance/SBOM\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Artifact provenance](../../docs/phase-15-bootstrap-and-self-hosting/210-boot8-bootstrap-artifact-provenance-specification.md)\n\n<!-- release-parent-reproducibility:start -->\nAdditional proposed source criteria (Open), from the published Release\n[task source](https://github.com/burn2delete/uniform/blob/df11890b21f71d3f246cc47e9f63d866239a0d68/specs/release-workflow/tasks.md).\nThe following closing-evidence text is preserved verbatim; the original\ncriterion below and existing governance interfaces remain required.\n\nRebuild identity and signature/provenance verification plus tamper rejection BOOT1/BOOT6/BOOT8: Retain locked dependencies, recipe and environment controls for time/locale/filesystem order/toolchain/network, compiler lineage and manifest/content-hash comparisons. Declare unsupported rebuild strategies; diverse rebuilds require independent toolchain identity. Reproducibility exceptions and accepted deltas require recorded review. Produce canonical signed provenance binding stage/artifact/source graph/compiler/lockfile/recipe/environment/dependencies/builder and conformance/equivalence/safety/SBOM/signature links. Auditor queries must traverse release compiler to seed inputs; permit only explicitly declared stage cycles. Reject lineage gaps, undeclared cycles, uncontrolled network inputs, noncanonical signing, missing required evidence, unexplained drift and revoked compiler/builder/dependency/signature inputs. Release extension release/final-rebuild-reproducibility: Rebuild the actual final gravity artifact at least twice from the recorded recipe, locked inputs and environment. Compare binary, provenance, SBOM, signing-record and command-contract evidence identities; retain both actual rebuild outputs and comparison report. Reject missing rebuilds/comparisons, unexplained drift and supplied-record substitution. Earlier hosted packaging reproducibility cannot close final release rebuilds. Release extension release/final-supply-chain-governance-bundle: Produce and validate the selected actual final release's provenance, SBOM, canonical signing records, release notes, target-support policy, compatibility, security-review and governance approval evidence. Bind records to actual binary, recipe/environment, source/compiler/dependency/target identities and accepted command evidence. Reject missing, stale, tampered, revoked or mismatched records, unsupported targets and governance gaps with applicable P18T06001-P18T06008 blockers. A hosted bundle is not final seedless evidence. Bootstrap criterion bootstrap/compiler-lineage-query: Execute the auditor query on a bootstrap compiler provenance graph and return which compiler built every queried stage/compiler artifact, recursively reaching its seed inputs. Record the queried artifact identities, traversed edges, compiler/source/lock/build/environment/evidence links and declared stage-cycle annotations; a provenance file alone is not a successful query. Reject missing compiler nodes/edges, broken release-to-seed traversal, undeclared cycles and an auditor query that cannot reconstruct a compiler's builder. Preserve explicitly declared stage cycles; do not reject them as undeclared cycles. Keep BOOT6002 and BOOT8002/BOOT8003/BOOT8007 with the offending artifact and edge. Required outputs: compiler lineage graph; auditor query index and successful traversal result; broken-edge/undeclared-cycle/query-failure fixtures and diagnostics. Bootstrap criterion bootstrap/locked-rebuild: Actually rebuild the declared bootstrap artifact from locked dependencies and its recorded recipe and environment, controlling time, locale, filesystem order, toolchain and network inputs. Run the applicable seed-built/self-built/clean-environment/diverse strategies, explicitly declaring unsupported strategies; a diverse report names the independent toolchain. Compare canonical manifests and relevant content hashes, retain compiler lineage, actual outputs and residual trusted components, and record policy-reviewed accepted deltas or a documented release reproducibility exception. Reject unlocked bootstrap dependencies, absent environment/lineage records, uncontrolled or unrecorded network input, unexplained hash drift and a diverse rebuild without independent toolchain identity. Revoked builders/dependencies/signatures block release. Exercise repeatable rebuild and each failure with BOOT1005/BOOT2005/BOOT6001-BOOT6006; the seed's declared host dependencies and runtime assumptions remain explicit. Required outputs: reproducible bootstrap recipe and controlled environment; real rebuild manifests/content comparisons and diverse-or-unsupported strategy report; accepted-delta/exception and residual-trust records; revocation and negative-fixture reports.\n<!-- release-parent-reproducibility:end -->\n\nClosing evidence: Rebuild identity and signature/provenance verification plus tamper rejection",
