  "- [ ] `release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/bind-each-claimed-component-to-exact-implementation-and-conformance` Bind each claimed component to exact implementation and conformance\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Overall roadmap](../../docs/implementation-roadmap.md)\n\n<!-- release-parent-coverage:start -->\nAdditional proposed source criteria (Open), from the published Release\n[task source](https://github.com/burn2delete/uniform/blob/df11890b21f71d3f246cc47e9f63d866239a0d68/specs/release-workflow/tasks.md).\nThe following closing-evidence text is preserved verbatim; the original\ncriterion below and existing governance interfaces remain required.\n\nComponent outcome receipts, positive/negative programs and explicit unsupported surface. Maintain the source-bound task/disposition matrix for all 240 original contracts and the separately declared release and Platform Product extensions. Keep every missing producer/checker/consumer interface, alias or split question, and architecture choice as finite named remaining work with criteria, dependencies and accountable role; an accountability link does not establish an implementation interface. Resolve those decisions and bind actual component evidence before claiming the corresponding release scope. This release-claim obligation does not block ordinary semantic development. Foundation requirement gravity/coverage-claim-slice: Publish each domain coverage claim as an exact behavior slice with source forms, profile, target/backend, provider/runtime assumptions, emitted artifacts and explicit unsupported boundaries, linked to the actual demonstrating product. Refusals: Reject a whole-domain claim supported only by a smaller slice, a missing profile/target, or a provider adapter presented as a complete replacement. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency