ersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open.\n\nSource obligation `language/effects/interpret-generator`: Interpret typed generator yield/send/completion and close operations under the handler's declared resume mode. Accept: Execute typed yield, send, completion and close operations under the declared generator resume mode; retain original labels, handler identity, captures and profile/grant facts. Reject: Reject wrong send/completion types, unsafe or repeated affine resumes, resume after close and unsupported profile/capture transfer. Required outputs: Generator request/result/continuation records and accepted yield/send/complete/close plus rejected unsafe-resume fixtures. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects3-check-legality-and-ordering, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open.\n\nL6 actual async/generator interpretation criterion (Open): Execute typed suspend/await, scheduler wakeup/cancel/timeout and generator yield/send/completion/close behavior using the selected supported runtime/profile, checked handler/resume/continuation contract, actual grants and capture/transfer facts. Preserve labels, handler identity, residual actions and real cleanup on cancellation, timeout and close. Refuse wrong request/send/completion/result types, unsupported scheduler/target/profile, missing authority, unsafe or repeated affine resumes, resume after cancel/completion/close and invalid captured-resource transfer. Multi-shot and serialized continuations require their explicit profile/proof/representation conditions. Emit actual request/result/state-transition, wakeup, cancel/timeout/close and cleanup traces plus refused boundary fixtures; a task graph, generic EffectRequest/Ef