  "- [ ] `mir/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/mir4-serialize-stable-modules` mir/4: Serialize stable modules\n\nCurrent evidence/status: Open; partial source evidence above is not closure\n\nDone when (yes/no): Round-trip operations and shared tables with deterministic identity and preserve analysis invalidation hooks.\n\n<!-- mir-canonical-serialization:start -->\nApply the [complete MIR source criteria](plan.md#complete-mir-source-criteria) within this existing task. Status remains Open; current independent review and implementation acceptance are pending.\n\nC11 serialization criterion (Open): Round-trip actual module/function/block/operation records, explicit control/data-flow edges and shared metadata tables with deterministic identity and valid origin/provenance links. Preserve the domain anchor's domain/anchor ID, MIR operation links, external semantic artifact, equivalence-proof reference and fallback MIR subgraph for EFIR/schema/workflow/HDL/query/GPU anchors as applicable; a domain payload cannot replace its semantic anchor. Preserve fact invalidation/replacement hooks rather than silently renewing a stale table or proof. Required outputs: serialized MIR/table/anchor artifacts and actual round-trip identity/edge/invalidation comparisons. Reject lost or substituted table IDs, origins, graph edges, anchor/proof/fallback references or stale-state erasure with applicable C11-MODULE/ORIGIN/DOMAIN/VERIFY. This representation/identity contract does not make EML tree identity mathematical equality or independently validate a proof provider.\n<!-- mir-canonical-serialization:end -->",
