fusion/denormal/approximation/provider/certificate facts through lowering or diagnose. ABI production, kernel/launch checks, buffer validity and actual Runtime transfers remain separate interfaces; a graph is not executed transfer evidence.\n\nCriterion profile-gap/gpu/host-device-boundary (Open): Input: Separate host orchestration and GPU kernel artifacts with argument address-space/layout/alignment/alias/lifetime and declared target feature/workgroup/grid/occupancy/launch configuration. Accept: Validate kernel-only legality, construct the typed host/device ABI boundary and transfer/lifetime records, and check target launch/features independently. Host profile remains explicit; device orchestration cannot import ambient host semantics into a kernel. Reject: Host IO/reflection/eval/allocation/GC/exceptions/ordinary threads in kernels, unsupported recursion/dispatch, missing argument or transfer boundary, invalid target or launch configuration. Required outputs: Host/device and target/launch/occupancy manifests, kernel IR, typed argument ABI and accepted/rejected kernel/launch/feature fixtures with kernel/buffer/address-space/origin context. Dependencies: backend-interface, lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower1-validate-lowering-inputs, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: [the preserved profile-interface context](plan.md#query-workflow-gpu-and-ui-source-context), mapping gpu/host-device-boundary; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/gpu/memory-synchronization (Open): Input: GPU buffers/slices and transfer/queue/kernel/barrier graph with ownership/lifetime/address-space/alignment/layout/alias/visibility and sharing-provider facts. A