  "- [ ] `kernel` Kernel / `kernel`\n\nStatus: Open\n\n<!-- platform-kernel-parent:start -->\n### Kernel parent proposed criteria\n\nCurrent refinement of the same Open `kernel` target-conformance task.\nResume the full body from\n[the published reconciliation](https://github.com/burn2delete/uniform/blob/2c88b9796fc0d0e6ca0bdc93cbfba41cb6921dcc/specs/platform-workflow/tasks.md#implementation-tasks).\nOnly profile/Domain context references change; other proposed text and the\noriginal short paragraph below remain preserved. Existing target maintainers\nretain ownership; no person, target/ABI, device or product is adopted here.\nThe [composition plan](plan.md#target-conformance-and-product-composition)\nkeeps Types/Legality/Auth checks, domain IR, Lower/Emit/backend products,\nactual Runtime/provider calls and target evidence distinct. A target slice\nis not the full Platform Product and does not receive acceptance by linking\nsource criteria. Current source/owner repartition and review remain pending.\n\nDeclared completion and remaining work: Adopt kernel ABI/execution model; implement initialization, memory and scheduling interface slice required by contract; verify unsafe boundaries, no hidden hosted services and artifact provenance. DOM3 acceptance requires typed syscall/user-pointer taint, capability and error mapping; raw-memory safe-wrapper/audit, allocation/panic/preemption/interrupt and ABI records. Exercise valid/invalid syscall, interrupt, allocator and page-table cases, reject ambient authority and hosted assumptions, and emit kernel object/boot image, syscall/interrupt tables, audit/capability/source maps and named emulator smoke evidence. Dependencies: profile legality, native lowering, ownership and runtime/FFI boundaries; OS product architecture remains unadopted ; P7 target conformance requires explicit page/frame/pinned/address-space/DMA and interrupt-safe allocator/failure/concurrency policy; reject hidden allocation/hosted services and unsupported