  "- [ ] `hardware` Hardware / `hardware`\n\nStatus: Open\n\n<!-- platform-hardware-parent:start -->\n### Hardware parent proposed criteria\n\nCurrent refinement of the same Open `hardware` target-conformance task.\nResume the full body from\n[the published reconciliation](https://github.com/burn2delete/uniform/blob/2c88b9796fc0d0e6ca0bdc93cbfba41cb6921dcc/specs/platform-workflow/tasks.md#implementation-tasks).\nOnly profile/Domain context references change; other proposed text and the\noriginal short paragraph below remain preserved. Existing target maintainers\nretain ownership; no person, target/ABI, device or product is adopted here.\nThe [composition plan](plan.md#target-conformance-and-product-composition)\nkeeps Types/Legality/Auth checks, domain IR, Lower/Emit/backend products,\nactual Runtime/provider calls and target evidence distinct. A target slice\nis not the full Platform Product and does not receive acceptance by linking\nsource criteria. Current source/owner repartition and review remain pending.\n\nDeclared completion and remaining work: Adopt clock/reset/HDL target contract; implement state-machine lowering and simulation; verify timing/reset invariants and reject illegal dynamic/runtime operations; emit traceable hardware artifact. DOM1 acceptance requires fixed synthesis-visible shapes, finite iteration and explicit CDC synchronizer/FIFO/handshake, proof or audit waiver; reject implicit widths/truncation, unsafe CDC, runtime-only constructs and nonfinite loops. Emit HDL, interface/clock/reset/timing records, source maps, testbench and simulation evidence. Exercise FIFO full/empty/reset/backpressure/data order plus counter and bus-peripheral fixtures. Dependencies: profile legality, HDL lowering, no-runtime and safety/proof consumers; target choice remains open ; P8 target conformance requires fixed-width shape/overflow checks, static unroll or structural conversion or rejection, explicit input-only nondeterminism, state-graph emission AND validation (initial/reset/transition/output/illegal-state behavior), clock/reset records (explicit uninitialized state allowed; unsafe power-on needs hardware audit), ports/protocols and CDC synchronizer/FIFO/handshake/proof or audited waiver. Reject runtime services and unmediated CDC. Capability targets must validate bounds/provenance/permissions/sealing/derivation, tags across register/memory/DMA/FIFO/bus/debug/port paths, declared compartment entry/return/shared-state authority and explicit temporal assumptions. Tag-destroying paths are marked and diagnosed unless source explicitly expects destruction; audited authority boundaries retain their conditions. A conforming target may declare no temporal revocation; stronger source requirements then reject or require separate proof. Emit source-mapped hardware IR/HDL, target/layout/tag/clock/reset/timing/port/compartment reports and positive/negative capability-target fixtures. ISA/product/fabrication selection remains unassessed. Criterion profile-gap/domain/hardware-cdc (Open): Input: Typed P8/DOM1 hardware graph with declared source/destination clocks and every cross-clock signal, port, bus or state edge. Accept: Associate each crossing with an explicit synchronizer, asynchronous FIFO, handshake, Gray-coded/equivalent proof or external hardware CDC waiver with audit record; validate the declared mediator and retain its source/proof/audit identity through hardware IR and HDL. Reject: Unmediated or unproven crossing, missing/incompatible clock-domain evidence and runtime synchronization substituted for hardware semantics. Required outputs: CDC graph/report, accepted synchronizer/FIFO/handshake fixtures and rejected unsafe crossing diagnostic with module/signal/state/span/clock/reset/HDL/missing-proof/remediation; preserve simulation, HDL source maps and conformance evidence from the DOM1 consumer. Dependencies: backend-hdl, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: [the preserved profile-interface context](plan.md#platform-source-context), mapping domain/hardware-cdc; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/hardware/capability-representation (Open): Input: Capability-hardware target manifest and typed pointer operation with word/address widths, bounds/granularity, provenance/derivation, permission bits, tag/seal/object/entry metadata. Accept: Select hardware capabilities only through the target manifest; type/layout-check representation and derivations for preserved provenance, enforced bounds and non-widening permissions. A conditional audited hardware authority boundary must retain its explicit preconditions and evidence. Reject: Pointers treated as integers, fabricated provenance, undeclared integer round-trip, unsupported representation or unchecked bounds/permission widening. Required outputs: Capability pointer/layout/metadata target manifest, legal derivation and rejected widening/representation fixtures, P8-CAPABILITY diagnostics identifying metadata field, module/signal/origin and target evidence. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types2-check-declared-abstractions, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, backend-hdl interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: [the preserved profile-interface context](plan.md#platform-source-context), mapping hardware/capability-representation; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/hardware/capability-tag-paths (Open): Input: Every capability-bearing register, memory, DMA, FIFO, bus/bridge, debug and external-port path with target tag/metadata propagation or destruction declaration. Accept: Preserve tags and