  "- [ ] `effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects3-check-legality-and-ordering` effects/3: Check legality and ordering\n\nCurrent evidence/status: Open; partial source evidence above is not closure\n\nDone when (yes/no): Reject undeclared effects and forbidden profile behavior, expose capability requirements, and preserve sequencing constraints without granting authority.\n\n\n<!-- effects-canonical-legality:start -->\nApply the [complete effect-checker source criteria](plan.md#complete-effect-checker-source-criteria) within this existing task. Status remains Open; current independent review and implementation acceptance are pending.\n\nC8 legality/capability/order criterion compiler/c8/capability-proof compiler/c8/effect-order (Open): Check the complete applicable intersection of function and namespace declarations, profile, package manifest, build/deployment grants, actual runtime/provider support and safety mode before MIR construction. Effects and capability sets remain distinct: derive required capabilities from registered effects and connect actual use to explicit authority evidence binding effect, core source, capability, provider, grant scope/principal/phase and status; reject missing or insufficient scoped grants before MIR. Backends/runtimes may narrow support but cannot grant authority absent from source/package/deployment. Authority evidence is not a safety proof; profile/safety/runtime-selection/audit consumers retain their own checks. Emit sequence, may-commute, must-not-duplicate, must-not-eliminate, resource acquire/release bracketing, volatile/MMIO/atomic and replay-order constraints; actual optimizers consume them before reordering/fusion/elimination. Required outputs: per-effect legality intersection, capability-proof records, ordering constraints and accepted/refused declaration/profile/grant/provider/safety fixtures, including resource/volatile/MMIO/atomic/workflow/AI order cases. Reject type-only legality, effect-name-derived grants