ndently of implicit host ABI, services and paths. Reject A cross build inherits host ABI/paths/default target assumptions. Emit Target-specific build/artifact identity and host-leakage rejection with PKG11002. Dependencies: PKG11, B1, R1. Criterion behavior/pkg11/per-target-evidence: accept Attach required conformance and support-level evidence separately to each target and expose every failing profile/target pair. Reject Default-target success hides a required target failure or a release claims support without its per-target conformance. Emit Per-target test/conformance reports, support table and PKG11006. Dependencies: PKG11, TEST3, TEST4, TEST6. Criterion behavior/pkg11/target-compatibility-admission: accept Validate profile/backend legality, dependency variants and capability availability for every concrete target before lowering. Reject A pair is unsupported, contradicts project profiles, lacks a dependency variant or assumes capabilities legal on another target. Emit Checked matrix, per-target graph/capability decision and PKG11001/PKG11003/PKG11004/PKG11008. Dependencies: PKG11, PKG5, P13, B1. Criterion behavior/pkg11/target-matrix-artifact: accept Normalize grouped declarations into concrete profile/backend/triple/ABI/calling-convention/runtime/features/dependency/capability/artifact/test/support entries and emit each target's manifests and support level. Reject Required target/ABI identity is missing, a matrix contradicts the project or a supported claim lacks its target-specific record. Emit Normalized matrix, dependency graph, capability summary, artifact/test/conformance manifests and supported/experimental/internal/build-only/unsupported table; PKG11005/PKG11008. Dependencies: PKG1, PKG11, R1, B1. Criterion behavior/pkg7/canonical-rebuild-comparison: accept Compare canonical manifests and actual content hashes for two locked builds under the same recipe, explaining only declared differences. Reject Verification compares filenames alone or ignores a changed canonical content/manifest identity. Emit Expected/actual digest lists and rebuild verification report; PKG7007. Dependencies: PKG3, PKG7. Criterion behavior/pkg7/deterministic-build-environment: accept Control source/project/lock/compiler/toolchain/graph/profile/target/environment/locale/timezone/order/timestamps/seeds/network/generated/blob/FFI inputs; normalize time/order/paths and seed or record randomness. Reject A reproducible build uses unlocked dependencies, unrecorded external reads/randomness, leaked host paths or generated source without generator/input hashes. Emit Controlled environment and input/output manifests, build recipe, exception list and PKG7002-PKG7006; changed compiler invalidates cache. Dependencies: PKG7, PKG2, PKG10. Criterion behavior/pkg7/nonreproducible-claim-boundary: accept Mark uncontrolled-input artifacts nonreproducible and list their exceptions explicitly. Reject A nonreproducible artifact satisfies a reproducible release/signing gate or a reproducibility claim lacks its recipe. Emit Nonreproducibility exception and release decision; PKG7001/PKG7008. Dependencies: PKG7, PKG12. Criterion behavior/pkg7/recorded-build-recipe: accept Emit a schema-valid release build recipe binding package/version, source/project/lock/compiler/toolchain, graph/task settings, concrete profile/target matrix, controlled environment/locale/timezone/traversal/timestamps/seeds/network, generator/input hashes, blobs/FFI inputs, expected artifact identities, output hashes and verification command or machine-readable equivalent. Rebuild twice under that exact recipe and compare canonical manifests and actual content hashes. For standard-library packages retain source commit, build graph, compiler, package lock, tests and policy-required signatures in the provenance record. Reject Reject a claimed reproducible release with no recipe, omitted or altered consumed inputs/outputs, unlocked dependencies, unrecorded network/randomness, host path leakage, missing 