  "- [ ] `release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/execute-staged-compiler-validation` Execute staged compiler validation\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [TEST13](../../docs/phase-14-testing-verification-and-conformance/202-test13-self-hosting-validation-plan.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Implement and execute the Execute staged compiler validation runner against actual declared owner interfaces, retaining the exact implementation/compiler/source/fixture/profile/target and applicable runtime/backend/provider identities. Run the named passing and failing cases; missing evidence is failure for the claimed scope, while inapplicable cases are explicitly reported. Source bootstrap/release-supply-chain: Require the active release policy's provenance, SBOM, signatures and reproducibility evidence on bootstrap release candidates. Concrete acceptance: Under the active release policy remove required provenance, SBOM, signature or reproducibility evidence, tamper the candidate identity, or revoke an input; reject the claim. Preserve TEST13 signed-or-otherwise-verifiable provenance: signing is mandatory only when that policy requires it. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source bootstrap/trust-reduction: Make the trusted compiler-source boundary and its change across a migration explicit and measurable. Concrete acceptance: Claim a reduced trusted base with no exact before/after compiler-source and host/toolchain inventory or with unchanged trust merely because source moved to Gravity; fail the claim and retain residual host dependencies. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test13/diagnostic-schema: Preserve self-hosted compiler diagnostic source spans/stable co