  "- [ ] `release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/execute-formal-evidence-checks` Execute formal evidence checks\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [TEST11](../../docs/phase-14-testing-verification-and-conformance/200-test11-formal-semantics-and-verification-plan.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Implement and execute the Execute formal evidence checks runner against actual declared owner interfaces, retaining the exact implementation/compiler/source/fixture/profile/target and applicable runtime/backend/provider identities. Run the named passing and failing cases; missing evidence is failure for the claimed scope, while inapplicable cases are explicitly reported. Source testing/test11/formal-obligations: Require declared and satisfied formal-profile proof obligations for release. Concrete acceptance: Run a formal-profile module with discharged and unmet obligations; reject the unmet claim, absent assumptions/trusted basis or prose-only release evidence. Executable tests remain complementary. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test11/pass-linkage: Bind optimization proofs to exact pass and before/after IR. Concrete acceptance: Check an optimization proof against exact pass/version and before/after IR; reject swapped inputs, absent transformation identity or an unchecked certificate. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test11/proof-identity: Record formal assumptions and trusted basis; proof artifacts identify claim ID, checker/version and input hash, rejecting unknown checkers or unstated assumptions. Concrete acceptance: Substitute checker name/version, input hash, claim ID or assumptions in a proof artifact; require checker rejection and retain its concrete result and trusted basis. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source testing/test11/report: Emit semantics artifacts, proof objects, certificate/checker/assumption manifests, counterexamples and proof invalidation reports across declared formal claim areas. Concrete acceptance: Remove semantics/proof/certificate/checker/assumption/counterexample/invalidation artifacts required by the claim; reject an uncheckable report rather than treating schema presence as a successful proof. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. This producer supplies conformance evidence; independent intermediate admission and final release remain separate consumers. Current implementation acceptance is unassessed.",
